## qf-bio2 | Quick-fire: biology 2 | bio | 0 | - | qf-bio
quiz 2 | What's the basic unit of life?
* The cell
o The atom
o The gene
o The organ
= Cell theory: all living things are made of cells.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which base pairs with adenine in DNA?
* Thymine
o Guanine
o Cytosine
o Uracil
= A–T and G–C. In RNA, uracil replaces thymine.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which organ produces insulin?
* The pancreas
o The liver
o The kidney
o The thyroid
= Beta cells in the islets of Langerhans.
> Next

quiz 3 | What's the largest living animal?
* The blue whale
o The African elephant
o The whale shark
o The giant squid
= Up to about 30 m and 150+ tonnes: the largest animal known to have ever lived.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which process do cells use to divide into two identical cells?
* Mitosis
o Meiosis
o Osmosis
o Fermentation
= Meiosis makes sex cells with half the chromosomes.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which scientist developed the first vaccine?
* Edward Jenner
o Louis Pasteur
o Alexander Fleming
o Robert Koch
= Smallpox, 1796. Pasteur later developed rabies and anthrax vaccines.
> Next

quiz 4 | How many bones in the adult human body?
* 206
o 300
o 186
o 256
= Babies have around 270–300; many fuse.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which part of the plant cell does photosynthesis?
* Chloroplasts
o Mitochondria
o Vacuoles
o Ribosomes
= Like mitochondria, they descend from once free-living bacteria.
> Next

quiz 4 | What do white blood cells mainly do?
* Fight infection
o Carry oxygen
o Clot blood
o Carry nutrients
= Platelets help clotting; red cells carry oxygen.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which animal has the longest known lifespan among vertebrates?
* The Greenland shark
o The tortoise
o The bowhead whale
o The elephant
= One was estimated at about 390 years old (with wide uncertainty).
> More quick-fire next

## qf-psy2 | Quick-fire: mind and brain | psych | 0 | - | qf-psy
quiz 2 | Which hormone is most associated with the sleep–wake cycle?
* Melatonin
o Insulin
o Adrenaline
o Oestrogen
= Released as it gets dark.
> Next

quiz 3 | The "fight or flight" response is driven mainly by…
* Adrenaline (epinephrine)
o Melatonin
o Serotonin
o Insulin
= Raises heart rate and blood sugar fast.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which lobe of the brain is mainly responsible for vision?
* Occipital
o Frontal
o Temporal
o Parietal
= At the back of the head.
> Next

quiz 3 | Imposter syndrome is…
* Feeling like a fraud despite evidence of competence
o Pretending to be someone else
o A formal psychiatric diagnosis
o Fear of crowds
= Common among high achievers. It's not an official diagnosis.
> Next

quiz 3 | The "Zeigarnik effect" says people remember…
* Unfinished tasks better than finished ones
o First impressions best
o Faces better than names
o Pleasant memories more
= Why cliffhangers stick. Replications are mixed, though.
> Next

quiz 4 | Who described the "hierarchy of needs"?
* Abraham Maslow
o Carl Rogers
o B. F. Skinner
o Jean Piaget
= 1943. The pyramid image was added later by others.
> Next

quiz 4 | Who proposed stages of cognitive development in children?
* Jean Piaget
o Sigmund Freud
o John Bowlby
o Lev Vygotsky
= Sensorimotor, preoperational, concrete operational, formal operational.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's "learned helplessness"?
* Giving up after repeated uncontrollable failures
o Learning by watching others
o Forgetting skills over time
o Relying on technology
= Seligman's experiments in the 1960s, later linked to depression.
> Quick-fire biology and mind complete

## qf-cs2 | Quick-fire: computing 2 | cs | 0 | - | qf-cs
quiz 3 | What does "AI" stand for?
* Artificial intelligence
o Automated integration
o Applied informatics
o Algorithmic interface
= Coined for the 1956 Dartmouth workshop.
> Next

quiz 3 | What is a "bug" in software?
* A mistake that makes a program behave incorrectly
o A virus
o A type of hardware
o A slow computer
= Debugging is finding and fixing them.
> Next

quiz 3 | What does "HTTP 404" mean?
* Page not found
o Server error
o Access forbidden
o Success
= 500 is a server error; 403 is forbidden; 200 is OK.
> Next

quiz 4 | What does a compiler do?
* Translates source code into machine code (or another lower-level form)
o Runs code line by line only
o Designs computer chips
o Stores files
= An interpreter runs code directly, line by line.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which company developed the first commercially successful graphical user interface for home computers?
* Apple (Macintosh, 1984), building on Xerox PARC's work
o Microsoft
o IBM
o Google
= Xerox PARC's Alto pioneered windows and the mouse in the 1970s.
> Next

quiz 4 | What does "SQL" query?
* Databases
o Websites' layout
o Image files
o Network speed
= Structured Query Language.
> Quick-fire computing complete
